      "classification": "core",
      "reviewed_domain": "Every positive rational shape A/B and success probability s/t with naturals A, B, s > 0 and s <= t, including s = t (point mass at zero) and shapes below one; every other integer input makes the source fail, so the domain is complete. The law is the canonical real-shape negative binomial NegativeBinomialShape.law with mass multichoose(A/B, n) (s/t)^(A/B) (1 - s/t)^n on failure counts n, output Val.int n. Arbitrary ENNReal credit, including infinity, is supported. No externally assumed sampler callbacks are needed.",
